# =============================================================================
# Trivy ignore list — accepted base-image vulnerabilities
# =============================================================================
# These CVEs originate from the Debian bookworm base of python:3.12-slim-bookworm
# (shared by the relay and ui images). All six have NO fixed Debian version
# available, so they cannot be resolved by patching, `apt-get upgrade`, or
# rebasing onto a newer base-image digest. They are accepted as documented risk.
#
# Trivy auto-loads this file from the working directory (repo checkout root);
# the fork-docker-build reusable workflow runs `trivy image` there, so listed
# CVEs are removed from the report before the CRITICAL gate counts them.
#
# Reviewed:      2026-07-02
# Next review:   2026-10-02  (re-check whether Debian shipped fixes; drop entries)
# Owner:         kb@de.bauer-group.com
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# zlib1g — integer overflow in minizip's zipOpenNewFileInZip4_6.
# Debian status: will_not_fix. The vulnerable minizip code is not compiled into
# Debian's zlib1g, so the library as shipped is not affected. Never fixed upstream.
CVE-2023-45853

# perl-base — heap buffer overflow compiling regexes on 32-bit builds only.
# Not applicable: the images are built for amd64 (64-bit). No fix available.
CVE-2026-8376

# perl-base — path traversal in Archive::Tar via crafted symlinks.
# Debian status: fix_deferred (no fix yet). relay/ui do not use Archive::Tar.
CVE-2026-42496

# perl-base — 16-bit overflow in Perl_study_chunk: an alternation of more than
# 65535 fixed-string branches compiled into a trie silently truncates the match
# table, yielding false positive/negative matches. Rated CRITICAL because it can
# undermine regex-based access control — in Perl code.
# Not applicable: nothing in relay/ui executes Perl at all; perl-base is only a
# transitive part of the Debian base image (the Alpine-based nginx image carries
# no perl and scans clean). Reaching the defect would additionally require a
# regex with >65535 fixed-string branches, which exists nowhere here.
# Fixed upstream in Perl 5.43.10; Debian bookworm is unfixed and so is sid, so
# no base-image digest bump or apt upgrade can resolve it.
CVE-2026-13221

# libsqlite3-0 — SQLite integer overflow. Status: affected, no fixed Debian
# version available. Re-evaluate on next review once Debian ships a patch.
CVE-2025-7458

# perl-base — signed integer overflow in Storable (< 3.41): deserializing a
# crafted SX_HOOK record panics. Rated CRITICAL because Storable::thaw on
# attacker-controlled blobs is a classic deserialization sink — in Perl code.
# Not applicable: same reasoning as CVE-2026-13221 — nothing in relay/ui
# executes Perl, and no Storable blob (trusted or not) is ever deserialized;
# perl-base is only a transitive part of the Debian base image.
# Debian bookworm ships 5.36.0-7+deb12u3 and is unfixed; trixie is unfixed too.
# Only sid/forky (perl 5.42.2-3) carries the fix, so no digest bump or
# apt-get upgrade on a bookworm base can resolve it.
# Added: 2026-08-01
CVE-2026-57433
